course: dictionary
lesson: 7566
title: Prescription: one word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one. «The doctor may write a prescription, the written permission for a medicine you cannot just buy.» The clues are doctor, write and medicine you cannot just buy, so here a prescription is a note from the doctor.
explain: The same word can also mean the medicine itself, given on a doctor's order. «When a doctor writes a prescription, an order for one medicine at one dose, the pharmacist checks the dose, your age, your allergies and your other medicines before handing it over.» The pharmacist checks and hands over the medicine, so the word here is about the medicine too.
explain: A third meaning is more formal: a firm rule or piece of advice about what should be done. Try the swap test: put your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense. If it fits, you have found the right meaning.
fact: A prescription is a note from a doctor, often called a GP, saying which medicine a patient needs.
fact: You take a prescription to a chemist or pharmacy to get the medicine.
fact: Some medicines need a prescription, and some can be bought without one.
fact: «Repeat prescription» means a prescription for medicine someone takes regularly, so they do not need to see the doctor every time.
fact: In a formal sense, a prescription is a firm rule or piece of advice about what should be done.
exercise: «The doctor may write a prescription, the written permission for a medicine you cannot just buy.» What is a prescription here? | A shop that sells sweets | A long walk to school | *A note from a doctor saying which medicine you need | A kind of bed
exercise: «A repeat prescription is for medicine someone takes regularly, so they do not need to see the doctor every time.» What does repeat prescription mean? | *Regular medicine that can be collected again without a new doctor visit | A card for the library | A rule that children must go to bed early | A letter to a teacher
exercise: Which word means the same as chemist? | *pharmacy | optician | doctor | prescription
test: «The pharmacist checks the dose, your age, your allergies and your other medicines before handing it over.» In this sentence, what does the pharmacist do before giving out the medicine? | Writes a story | Sells a bike | Asks for a bus ticket | *Checks the dose and your other medicines
test: «Her coach gave a firm prescription: rest every day.» What does prescription mean here? | A kind of football | A medicine in a bottle from a shop | A picture of a horse | *A firm piece of advice about what should be done
exam: Ella asks what a prescription is. Which answer is best? | A kind of cough | *A note from a doctor saying which medicine you need, to take to the pharmacy | A shop that sells medicine | A word that means cheap
